<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States Declaration of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1776">1776</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Declaration of Independence was adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-continental-congress">Second Continental Congress</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> on 4 July 1776. Drafted mainly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>, it announced that the thirteen American colonies were independent states no longer bound to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, listed grievances against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> and set out the principle that governments rest on the consent of the governed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states-declaration-of-independence.jpg" alt="United States Declaration of Independence" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original: w:Second Continental Congress; reproduction: William Stone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_Declaration_of_Independence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
